WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.420
Every cell in a cluster can audition.

2
00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:07.420
What gives them that ability?

3
00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.870
The proneural genes were found in the fly.

4
00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:15.210
Two of them, achaete and scute, sit side by side on a chromosome.

5
00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:18.810
They are needed for the bristles on the fly's back.

6
00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:22.413
Predict. Remove these genes.

7
00:00:23.393 --> 00:00:24.653
What happens to the bristles?

8
00:00:25.593 --> 00:00:27.193
Then switch them on in extra places.

9
00:00:33.683 --> 00:00:35.723
Remove them, and bristles are missing.

10
00:00:36.723 --> 00:00:39.703
Switch them on in extra places, and extra bristles form.

11
00:00:40.717 --> 00:00:44.117
A related gene, atonal, was found in 1993.

12
00:00:45.217 --> 00:00:47.417
It does the same job for chordotonal organs.

13
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:50.480
These are internal stretch receptors.

14
00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:55.270
So different proneural genes start different kinds of sense organ.

15
00:00:56.333 --> 00:01:00.053
Force achaete-scute on, and only external sense organs form.

16
00:01:01.173 --> 00:01:04.073
Force atonal on, and mostly chordotonal organs form.

17
00:01:05.066 --> 00:01:08.366
A year later, atonal was shown to be needed for R8.

18
00:01:09.146 --> 00:01:11.886
That is the founding photoreceptor of each eye unit.

19
00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.160
Without atonal, no R8 forms.

20
00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.880
The other seven photoreceptors, which R8 recruits, do not form either.

21
00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:25.840
All these genes encode the same kind of protein: a basic helix-loop-helix (bHLH)

22
00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:26.920
transcription factor.

23
00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.720
The helix-loop-helix part lets two proteins pair.

24
00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:34.880
The basic part grips DNA at a short sequence called an E-box.

25
00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:38.270
A proneural protein works with a partner.

26
00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:41.190
In the fly, that partner is Daughterless.

27
00:01:42.183 --> 00:01:44.903
In vertebrates, the partners are called E proteins.

28
00:01:46.116 --> 00:01:48.916
Vertebrates have relatives of both fly families.

29
00:01:49.856 --> 00:01:52.316
Ascl1 is related to achaete-scute.

30
00:01:53.266 --> 00:01:57.166
The Neurogenins, and a gene called Atoh1, are related to atonal.

31
00:01:58.166 --> 00:02:00.206
So what decides where a cluster forms?

32
00:02:01.126 --> 00:02:04.686
In the embryo, clusters still form in the right places without Notch.

33
00:02:05.906 --> 00:02:09.166
Regulatory DNA around the achaete-scute genes sets the map.

34
00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:12.940
That map was worked out mostly on the notum and wing.

35
00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.680
There, Notch also helps shape the broader proneural stripes.

36
00:02:17.733 --> 00:02:19.453
That answers the first puzzle.

37
00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:23.193
Proneural factors make a cluster able to become neural.

38
00:02:24.613 --> 00:02:25.833
Regulatory DNA places it.

39
00:02:26.716 --> 00:02:28.456
Proneural factors say who may.

40
00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:30.396
Notch will say who does.
